Bill Wayne wrote:
> I've recently gotten myself addicted to nethack. I've tried to stay
> away from spoilers, so I was pretty excited with the current game,
> which was a human monk.
>
> Leprechaun Hall on DL 9, Treasure Zoo on DL 10, and Vault on DL 11
> meant I could affod protection twice. There was also a coaligned altar
> on DL 10, so by saccing all of the zoo occupants I got sunsword as an
> artifact. It remained my light source throughout the game. Protection
> pushed my AC down to -2, which I think is pretty good for mid-game.

You should be able to do better if you'd bought two levels of
protection.  Buying protection twice will get you like 4 AC, plus 4 for
iron helm/shoes, plus 3 for the robe, plus 1 for a small shield, plus 3
for the starting gloves and you're at AC -5 without any enchantment.
By trying on all the uncursed armor you find you can easily have 5 or
more extra AC on top of that by the time you reach Sokoban--you might
lose a point if you find speed boots or something, but being in the -5
to -10 range is what I look for by the time I've finished Sokoban and
Minetown with a monk (obviously other classes add mithril or other
armor on top of that).

