The loads of food is to offset how hard it is to find anything you can
eat w/o taking alignment hits.  I find monks are the only class I
commonly have food problems with, though heading for sokoban first
helps.

> Is there any general advice anybody has about the midgame? Nethack has
> sucked up a huge portion of my time, so I'd like to get better at it.

Try to get reflection and magic resistance ASAP.  Check for magic lamps
in shops and bless them up, and feel free to blow them on wishes since
you'll be getting your quest artifact eventually to help with vision.
I like getting the luckstone from mine's end before proceeding below
the Sokoban level, and maxing my luck.

Monks are at a disadvantage getting the key resistances (reflection/MR)
since they don't wear armor, so feel free to blow wishes on them.
Amulet of Reflection, cloak of magic resistance, shield of reflection
are your non-artifact sources, and they all have drawbacks (shield
hurts spellcasting and leaves you wide open if you do take it off,
cloak displaces the robe, amulet prevents you from getting amulet of
ESP or life saving).

I find wishing for a MR-granting artifact is a priority (and it's
certainly a must if you want to keep your robe).  If you don't like
wishing for artifacts, bear in mind that you're basically going to have
to find/wish for a cloak of MR at some point (relying on your Quest
artifact is quite dangerous).



